WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.400 --> 00:00:03.467
-Welcome to our show.
-Yeah, this is crazy.

00:00:03.467 --> 00:00:05.667
This is like, "Oh, my God.
It's Jimmy Fallon."

00:00:05.667 --> 00:00:07.467
-No.
This is Matthias Schweighofer.

00:00:07.467 --> 00:00:09.100
This is finally -- We meet.

00:00:09.100 --> 00:00:10.767
-By the way, you say
"Schweighofer" like --

00:00:10.767 --> 00:00:12.968
This is like really --
It's a hard word to say.

00:00:12.968 --> 00:00:14.934
Like, your last name.
Even, you know...

00:00:14.934 --> 00:00:16.434
-Shwegg...
-Hoffer. It's fantastic.

00:00:16.434 --> 00:00:18.000
-Schweighofer. Yeah.
-Yeah, it's great.

00:00:18.000 --> 00:00:19.667
-I have a little --
I'm half Irish, half German.

00:00:19.667 --> 00:00:21.734
-Yes, and you --
-Yeah, yeah.

00:00:21.734 --> 00:00:24.000
-So that's the Irish part of me
saying "Shwegg."

00:00:24.000 --> 00:00:25.467
[ Laughter ]

00:00:25.467 --> 00:00:29.400
My -- My grandmother
came over to America

00:00:29.400 --> 00:00:31.200
at Ellis Island as a baby.

00:00:31.200 --> 00:00:34.634
Schalla was her last name,
from Bremen.

00:00:34.634 --> 00:00:36.534
-Okay, Bremen. Yeah.
-"Bremen."

00:00:36.534 --> 00:00:38.868
-"Brayman." Yeah, Bremen.
It's like "Brayman."

00:00:38.868 --> 00:00:40.234
-Of course.
-You say it's a --

00:00:40.234 --> 00:00:42.067
-Of course. I know what
you're talking about.

00:00:42.067 --> 00:00:45.033
I was doing a lot of research
on you because I was a fan

00:00:45.033 --> 00:00:46.234
from "Army of the Dead,"

00:00:46.234 --> 00:00:48.901
but then I saw this headline
and I loved it.

00:00:48.901 --> 00:00:50.467
"Matthias Schweighofer:

00:00:50.467 --> 00:00:53.234
They call me the Justin
Timberlake of Germany."

00:00:53.234 --> 00:00:56.501
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:56.501 --> 00:00:58.767
And I feel --
I feel it a little bit.

00:00:58.767 --> 00:01:01.334
But explain again why.
-I don't know.

00:01:01.334 --> 00:01:04.033
If I -- if someone said that
in Germany or --

00:01:04.033 --> 00:01:07.334
or if I said that
in an interview...

00:01:07.334 --> 00:01:10.133
-[ Laughter ]
-Either way. It counts.

00:01:10.133 --> 00:01:13.367
Someone said it, right?
-You know --

00:01:13.367 --> 00:01:14.834
-This --
-Sorry. No.

00:01:14.834 --> 00:01:16.734
No, really, it's because
there was a time, you know,

00:01:16.734 --> 00:01:18.701
like, I'm -- I think
I'm a good dancer,

00:01:18.701 --> 00:01:22.534
but a kind of shy dancer.
-What is shy dancing?

00:01:22.534 --> 00:01:23.667
-Do you know like --

00:01:23.667 --> 00:01:26.467
Shy dancer is, you know,
somewhere in the shades.

00:01:26.467 --> 00:01:28.300
You really --
You think you're like --

00:01:28.300 --> 00:01:30.834
Quest, can you give us a beat?
What would a shy --

00:01:30.834 --> 00:01:32.300
-Like, when you, uh...

00:01:32.300 --> 00:01:34.834
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:01:34.834 --> 00:01:36.968
It's like...

00:01:36.968 --> 00:01:41.234
♪♪

00:01:41.234 --> 00:01:45.501
♪♪

00:01:45.501 --> 00:01:47.501
[ Laughter ]

00:01:47.501 --> 00:01:49.501
-[ Speaking indistinctly ]

00:01:49.501 --> 00:01:51.300
[ Laughter ]

00:01:51.300 --> 00:01:52.601
-I like the kick at the end.

00:01:52.601 --> 00:01:56.133
Why not a little pop
to the end there? Yeah.

00:01:56.133 --> 00:01:58.400
I'm just so happy that you're

00:01:58.400 --> 00:02:00.067
kind of exploding
here in America

00:02:00.067 --> 00:02:01.801
and people are getting
to see how --

00:02:01.801 --> 00:02:04.267
how charming you are,
but also how talented you are.

00:02:04.267 --> 00:02:06.667
You directed this film,
as well as acting in it.

00:02:06.667 --> 00:02:08.634
"Army of Thieves."

00:02:08.634 --> 00:02:11.167
And here are some reviews.
Early reviews that came out.

00:02:11.167 --> 00:02:13.434
Someone says, "In the early
scenes of his English language

00:02:13.434 --> 00:02:17.067
directing debut, he occasionally
recalls Wes Anderson.

00:02:17.067 --> 00:02:19.834
He even has echoes
of Martin Scorsese's

00:02:19.834 --> 00:02:21.734
clockwork studies in 'Hugo.'"

00:02:21.734 --> 00:02:23.400
-Isn't that cool?

00:02:23.400 --> 00:02:25.067
-You just got compared
to Wes Anderson

00:02:25.067 --> 00:02:26.400
and Martin Scorsese.

00:02:26.400 --> 00:02:29.334
-I could be
Wes Matthias Scorsese.

00:02:29.334 --> 00:02:31.367
-Wow. That is --
That is -- Yeah.

00:02:31.367 --> 00:02:33.133
You should think about that.

00:02:33.133 --> 00:02:34.734
So you're working
with Zack Snyder, right?

00:02:34.734 --> 00:02:36.634
So that's a big break
right there.

00:02:36.634 --> 00:02:38.634
But then you start doing --
you start doing the scenes,

00:02:38.634 --> 00:02:40.000
and we had Tig Notaro
on the show,

00:02:40.000 --> 00:02:41.400
and we were talking
about the movie.

00:02:41.400 --> 00:02:43.634
And I watched the movie,
and I go --

00:02:43.634 --> 00:02:45.334
She steals every scene.
I love her.

00:02:45.334 --> 00:02:46.567
Then you come in.

00:02:46.567 --> 00:02:48.100
I go, "Who is this guy?"
-Yeah.

00:02:48.100 --> 00:02:49.534
-And you just stole every scene,

00:02:49.534 --> 00:02:51.334
and you're just
charming and funny.

00:02:51.334 --> 00:02:52.901
-Yeah, it was -- it was so --

00:02:52.901 --> 00:02:56.434
You know, I was so happy
about the critics to be --

00:02:56.434 --> 00:02:59.400
"You know, this German guy,
he's actually really funny.

00:02:59.400 --> 00:03:01.467
He has a cool sense of humor."

00:03:01.467 --> 00:03:03.367
And, you know,
because I always love --

00:03:03.367 --> 00:03:04.901
You know, American comedy,

00:03:04.901 --> 00:03:07.033
it's like, you know,
when I was younger --

00:03:07.033 --> 00:03:09.067
Because I was born behind
the wall,

00:03:09.067 --> 00:03:12.901
then the wall came down
in East Germany, so --

00:03:12.901 --> 00:03:14.734
And then the world came down,
and, you know, everything

00:03:14.734 --> 00:03:17.067
from America has swept over,
and I loved it.

00:03:17.067 --> 00:03:18.834
-What were you watching?
What were you into?

00:03:18.834 --> 00:03:20.300
-"Fresh Prince," you know?
And --

00:03:20.300 --> 00:03:22.467
-Yeah, of course.
Of course, yeah.

00:03:22.467 --> 00:03:24.667
-Yeah, yeah.
-"Fresh Prince." Yeah.

00:03:24.667 --> 00:03:25.901
-I loved it.

00:03:25.901 --> 00:03:27.501
-It all begins
with "fresh Prince."

00:03:27.501 --> 00:03:30.834
-I couldn't understand it
because I had no English.

00:03:30.834 --> 00:03:32.367
But it was like this.

00:03:32.367 --> 00:03:35.200
[ Singing theme song
in gibberish ]

00:03:35.200 --> 00:03:36.567
You know, Will Smith's like...

00:03:36.567 --> 00:03:39.334
[ Both singing in gibberish ]

00:03:39.334 --> 00:03:41.400
-Yeah.
-And that was great.

00:03:41.400 --> 00:03:44.100
And then I saw "E.T." for the
first time, and I thought --

00:03:44.100 --> 00:03:46.100
"You know, the wall came down.

00:03:46.100 --> 00:03:49.801
And in America, it's possible
to talk to aliens."

00:03:49.801 --> 00:03:51.801
[ Laughter ]

00:03:51.801 --> 00:03:53.334
-Anything is possible.

00:03:53.334 --> 00:03:55.400
Anything is possible
in America, yes.

00:03:55.400 --> 00:03:56.667
-And I loved it.

00:03:56.667 --> 00:03:58.534
And so I started to dream big,
and here we are.

00:03:58.534 --> 00:04:01.400
-Ah. Well, I'm so excited.
I'm happy that you're here.

00:04:01.400 --> 00:04:03.534
I'm happy that we're --
-Thank you.

00:04:03.534 --> 00:04:05.133
-We meet each other
and we're friends now.

00:04:05.133 --> 00:04:08.868
-Yeah, we're friends. Yeah.
-I want to show everyone a clip.

00:04:08.868 --> 00:04:12.133
Here's Matthias Schweighofer
in "Army of Thieves."

00:04:12.133 --> 00:04:13.934
Take a look of this.

00:04:13.934 --> 00:04:16.000
-I just want to clarify
once more.

00:04:16.000 --> 00:04:17.367
-Zip it!
-Okay.

00:04:17.367 --> 00:04:19.334
Okay. If you say so.

00:04:19.334 --> 00:04:22.801
[ Beeping ]

00:04:22.801 --> 00:04:27.234
♪♪

00:04:27.234 --> 00:04:29.767
[ Clicking ]

00:04:29.767 --> 00:04:33.100
♪♪

00:04:33.100 --> 00:04:34.534
[ Thud ]

00:04:34.534 --> 00:04:41.400
♪♪

00:04:41.400 --> 00:04:42.868
[ Thud ]

00:04:42.868 --> 00:04:47.934
♪♪

00:04:47.934 --> 00:04:49.701
[ Thud ]

00:04:49.701 --> 00:04:53.567
♪♪

00:04:53.567 --> 00:04:55.434
[ Clicking ]

00:04:57.434 --> 00:05:01.367
-Ladies and gentlemen!
There's a new kid in town!

00:05:01.367 --> 00:05:04.200
-That's right!
There's a new kid in town.

00:05:04.200 --> 00:05:06.534
Matthias Schweighofer!

00:05:06.534 --> 00:05:09.634
"Army of Thieves" begins
steaming on Netflix tomorrow.

00:05:09.634 --> 00:05:11.868
Hello to all our friends
in Germany.

00:05:11.868 --> 00:05:13.968
Thank you so much for watching.

